TITLE:: RLLattice
summary:: A walk shown on HomewareVisuals' lattice page: the plane of fifths and thirds, and the torus of a division
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLWalk, Classes/RLWalker, Classes/RCVisuals, Classes/RLJust, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
HomewareVisuals' page code::/lattice/:: draws a walk on triads twice: on the left on the lattice of fifths and major thirds, where it really goes; on the right on the torus an equal division folds that lattice into, one cell whose sides are two commas the division tempers out. A walk that closes in the division comes back to its triangle on the right, and has moved by a comma on the left.

The page is sent triads of code::RLJust([3, 5])::, or tetrads of code::RLJust([3, 5, 7]):: (4:5:6:7 and its inversion, link::Classes/RLChordSpace#*tetrads::). For tetrads the lattice has a third, short axis for the harmonic seventh, a tetrad is a triangle with its fourth point joined to the three others, and the right panel shows the division's steps round a circle with the chord's four tones: the torus of that lattice has three dimensions and is not drawn.

A walk of an equal division is shown by its lift from 1/1 (link::#*show:: does it); a walker takes a shadow on the lattice (link::Classes/RLWalker#-follow::). Messages go through link::Classes/RCVisuals:: (code::/lattice/config::, code::/lattice/clear::, code::/lattice/chord::, code::/lattice/tetrad::; the page's engine, code::public/lib/lattice-viz.js:: in HomewareVisuals, has the protocol).

code::
~ctx = RLChordContext(RLChordSpace.triads(RLEDO(12)));
~pump = RLWalk(~ctx, ~ctx.space.major(0), [\R, \L, \R, \P, \R, \L, \R, \L]);
RLLattice.show(~pump);                     // the division, then the nine chords of the lift

// tetrads: two fifths and two major thirds up, a harmonic seventh down. 31 steps close it; on the lattice
// it ends 225/224 from its start
~four = RLChordContext(RLChordSpace.tetrads(RLEDO(31)));
RLLattice.show(RLWalk(~four, ~four.space.otonal, [\K12, \K01, \K12, \K01, \K12, \K02, \K12, \K02, \K01, \K13]));

// a walker in a beat of reCurrent: each chord reaches the page when its sound starts
~walker = RLWalker(~ctx, ~ctx.space.major(0), [60, 64, 67], 8.1757989156, 0.75).follow;
RLLattice.config(~ctx.system);  RLLattice.clear;
~beat = ~song.layer(\core).addBeat(\harmony, [instrument: \default, dur_flex: 2,
	freq: ~walker.asPattern(Pseq([\R, \L], inf)), lattice: RLLattice.pfunc(~walker)]);
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: config
Tell the page what folds the lattice: an link::Classes/RLEDO:: (its steps, those of its fifth, of its major third and of its harmonic seventh: the torus, or the circle for tetrads), an link::Classes/RLTempered:: of one comma of the lattice of 3 and 5 (the comma: the cylinder, meantone's a strip along the fifths with its notes spelled along that chain), or nil (the right panel stays empty).
code::
~mean = RLChordContext(RLChordSpace.triads(RLTempered.meantone));
RLLattice.show(RLWalk(~mean, ~mean.space.major, [\P, \L, \P, \L, \P, \L]));     // ends on Dbb major, a diesis above C
::

METHOD:: clear
Forget the walk drawn.

METHOD:: chord
Send one chord of the lattice.
argument:: chord
A triad of code::RLJust([3, 5]):: or a tetrad of code::RLJust([3, 5, 7])::; anything else is an Error.
argument:: k
The number of the step.

METHOD:: args
The arguments of the page's message for a chord: code::[fifths, thirds, type, step]:: for a triad (code::/lattice/chord::), code::[fifths, thirds, sevenths, type, step]:: for a tetrad (code::/lattice/tetrad::).

METHOD:: path
The page's message for a chord: code::'/lattice/chord':: or, for a chord of four tones, code::'/lattice/tetrad'::.

METHOD:: isTetrad
Whether a chord has four tones.

METHOD:: just
The context of the lattice that lifts a chord's walks: triads on code::RLJust([3, 5])::, tetrads on code::RLJust([3, 5, 7])::.

METHOD:: show
A whole walk at once: the division, a clear, then every chord. A walk of an equal division is lifted to the lattice from 1/1; a walk of the lattice is shown as it is, with the division given. Returns the walk shown.

METHOD:: pfunc
For a beat or a Pbind: a key whose value sends the walker's place on the lattice when each event's sound starts. Put it after code::freq::. The walker stands on the lattice, or follows there (link::Classes/RLWalker#-follow::).
